+### `EXL3_BC_MLP_MAX_ROWS` (default: `32`)
+
+Most rows (bsz x q_len) the graphed dense GatedMLP path (`BC_GatedMLP`) takes; larger inputs run
+the eager path. The limit is 32 (`MLP_MAX_ROWS`, which also sizes the shared static scratch), so a
+batched speculative verify up to 4 x 8 rows stays graphed; `8` restores the previous limit.
+Read at import.
+
 ### `EXL3_BC_GDN_REPLAY` (default: `1`)
 
 With `EXL3_GDN_REPLAY=1`, the verify pass also runs as the graph-captured C++ call. Its conv
@@ -361,6 +368,18 @@ pipeline everywhere, for A/B testing.
 Override the path of the on-disk autotune cache for the cooperative GEMM kernels (kernel shape
 selection results, persisted across runs).
 
+## Speculative decoding
+
+### `EXL3_DRAFT_ROW_BUDGET` (default: `0`, off)
+
+Occupancy-aware draft length. A batched verify forward is (active sequences) x (draft + 1) rows.
+With a budget N, each round drafts `min(num_draft_tokens, N // sequences - 1)` tokens, at least 1,
+so the verify stays within N rows (the multi-row GEMV's fast range: 32 on gfx12 with
+`EXL3_GEMV_WMMA=1`). For example, `16` with 7 draft tokens drafts 7 at one or two jobs and 3 at four.
+DFlash2 then also runs the head and selector over only the rows it uses. Applies to every draft
+mode (DFlash2, draft model, MTP, n-gram). `0` or unset leaves the draft length alone. Read when the
+Generator is created.
+
